## 1. Fundamentals

### What is Snowflake?
A fully managed cloud data platform (SaaS) on AWS, Azure or GCP. No hardware, no indexes, no vacuuming, no manual partitioning.
**Key idea:** storage and compute are separate – you scale and pay for each independently.

### Editions (each includes the one above)
| Edition | Adds |
|---|---|
| Standard | Core platform, Time Travel up to 1 day |
| Enterprise | Multi-cluster warehouses, Time Travel up to 90 days, masking & row access policies, materialized views, search optimization, query acceleration, ACCESS_HISTORY, data metric functions |
| Business Critical | HIPAA/PCI support, Tri-Secret Secure (customer key), AWS PrivateLink, failover/failback |
| Virtual Private Snowflake | Fully isolated environment |

Healthcare (PHI) workloads normally need **Business Critical**.

### Object hierarchy
```
ORGANIZATION
 └── ACCOUNT (one cloud + region)
      ├── Users, Roles, Warehouses, Resource Monitors, Integrations, Network Policies
      └── DATABASE
           └── SCHEMA
                ├── Tables, Views, Stages, File Formats, Sequences
                ├── Streams, Tasks, Pipes, Dynamic Tables, Alerts
                └── Procedures, Functions, Policies, Tags, Secrets
```
Fully qualified name: `database.schema.object` (e.g. `sales_db.raw.raw_orders`).

